<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rashidi dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1836">1836</a>–<a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as House of Rashid, Al Rashid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rashidi dynasty, of the Shammar tribe, ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Jabal Shammar in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> from its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hail">Ha'il</a> between 1836 and 1921. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-rashid">Muhammad ibn Rashid</a> it defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-saud">Al Saud</a> and dominated central Arabia, with Ottoman support. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Ibn Saud</a> retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a> in 1902 the Rashidis were steadily pushed back, and Ha'il fell to him in 1921.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rashidi-dynasty.jpg" alt="Rashidi dynasty" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guilherme Paula · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Emirate_of_Ha%27il.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
